Experiment 1 — Matrix Multiplication

Aim:
To implement and analyze 4000 × 4000 matrix multiplication using different parallel computing approaches.

Experiment:
Matrix multiplication is implemented using:

Sequential CPU execution

OpenMP shared-memory parallelism

MPI distributed-memory parallelism

CUDA GPU parallelism


The sequential implementation provides the baseline, while OpenMP, MPI, and CUDA are used to demonstrate parallel execution and performance improvement. All implementations produce the verification result C[0][0] = 4000.00. 

Results:

Method	Execution Time	Speedup

Sequential	244.120000 s	1.00×
OpenMP	30.830434 s	7.92×
MPI	92.979510 s	2.63×
CUDA	0.165004 s	1479.48×


The experiment demonstrates how the same matrix multiplication workload can be executed using sequential, shared-memory, distributed-memory, and GPU-based parallel computing models. 